<HandSpinnerLayout title="Hand Spinner Support — Controls & purchases | nuunnu.com" description="Get started with Hand Spinner for Mac. Learn the trackpad controls, leave play mode, move the spinner and restore your purchased skins.">
  <header class="legal-heading"><p class="eyebrow">HAND SPINNER / SUPPORT</p><h1>Need a hand?</h1><p>First spin, a new skin, or something that doesn’t feel right.<br />Here’s where to start.</p></header>
  <div class="legal-body">
    <section>
      <h2>Your first spin.</h2>
      <p>Hand Spinner requires macOS 14 or later. The Mac App Store release is coming soon.</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Launch Hand Spinner. On the first launch, read the short guide and choose <strong>START SPINNING</strong>. You can reopen it from the menu-bar icon → <strong>How to Play…</strong>.</li>
        <li>Press <kbd>Option</kbd> + <kbd>Space</kbd> to show or hide the spinner. You can also use the menu-bar icon to open it.</li>
        <li>Click the spinner to enter play mode. The pointer is hidden while you play.</li>
        <li>Hold <kbd>Space</kbd> and move one finger on the trackpad. Stop moving to let it coast; release Space when you like. You don’t need to keep swiping.</li>
        <li>Add another push in the same direction to speed it up. Move against the rotation to brake or reverse.</li>
        <li>Press <kbd>Escape</kbd> to leave play mode and restore the pointer. Once you’re out of play mode, drag the spinner to move it.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>If the controls don’t respond.</h2>
      <p>Make sure you have clicked the spinner and are holding Space while moving one finger. Press Escape to reset play mode, then click the spinner again.</p>
      <p>If Option-Space is used by another app or a macOS keyboard shortcut, open Hand Spinner from its menu-bar icon instead. Review the conflicting shortcut in System Settings or that app’s settings.</p>
      <p>If the pointer does not return after Escape, use Option-Space to hide the overlay. If necessary, press Command-Option-Escape and force quit Hand Spinner, then relaunch it.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Skins &amp; restoring purchases.</h2>
      <p>The Standard skin is included free. The optional <strong>1998 Translucent Pack</strong> unlocks Atomic Purple, Glacier Blue, Smoke and Tangerine with a one-time purchase, not a subscription.</p>
      <p>Open the menu-bar icon → <strong>1998 Translucent Pack…</strong> to preview the skins. Apple shows the final price before you confirm payment.</p>
      <p>To restore an earlier purchase, sign in to the Mac App Store with the same <strong>Apple Account</strong> used to buy the pack, then choose <strong>Restore Purchases</strong> in the skin-pack window. An internet connection may be needed.</p>
      <p>If you cancel Apple’s purchase dialog, no new skin pack is unlocked. If approval is pending, wait for Apple’s confirmation. If the product is unavailable or a purchase fails, check your App Store account and connection, then try again later. Don’t keep buying the pack to fix a restore problem—contact support instead.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Tell us what happened.</h2>
      <p>Email your Mac model, macOS version, Hand Spinner version and the steps that led to the issue. A screenshot can help; remove any personal information first.</p>
      <p>Never send your Apple password, payment-card details or verification codes.</p>
